config FIBRIL_CAN_NODE_CAN_DIAG
	bool "Report this board's CAN health on the bus"
	default y
	depends on FCAN_TRANSPORT
	imply STATS
	imply CAN_STATS
	help
	  Publish the CanPortDiag and CanHubDiag block types (fibril_can's
	  zephyr/schema/can_diag.yaml): each CAN controller's state, error
	  counters, bus-off count and CAN_STATS, and a hub's forwarding
	  counters. The bridge turns them into /<node>/can{i}/diag and
	  /<node>/can_hub/diag.

	  Unlike the other functions this one is not described in the
	  devicetree. The transport decides the instances: one CanPortDiag for
	  the zephyr,canbus controller, or one per hub peer plus a CanHubDiag.
	  On by default so every board reports; turning it off removes the
	  instances from the schema.

	  STATS and CAN_STATS are implied rather than selected, so a board
	  short of RAM can drop the error counters (stats_valid then reads
	  false) and keep the rest.
